# Starter ship blueprint ? NATIVE 8? (2026-08-20). EDIT ME ? the game and
# the 8? startup test load this file; what you draw here is what spawns.
# The frozen 1? ancestor lives in tests/fixtures/starter_1x.ship for the
# legacy test scene only.
#
# One character per block:
#   .  empty        #  hull         G  gasbag (lift, free)
#   E  engine       H  helm         B  ballast
#   W  blubber      D  door (spawns closed; F opens/closes)
#   -  platform (S+jump drops through)   |  strut (no collision)
#   ^ v < > P V  propeller ? ONE component, axis comes from mounting:
#                 side neighbour = horizontal, above/below = vertical
#
# TRUE COMPONENT FOOTPRINTS (owner survey, WORLD_SPEC.md): engine 4x4,
# door 1-wall-deep x 8 tall, propeller 6x2 / 2x6 by mounting, helm 4x7,
# turret 2x8. A component's output and mass are its RATING at this
# scale (BlockDB.FOOTPRINT_8X), never its cell count ? so the smaller
# footprints fly, power and weigh exactly like the old uniform slabs.
# Bulk blocks (hull, gasbag, ballast, planks, struts) stay per-cell.
#
# Layout is the same vessel as ever: gasbag canopy; bow cabin with the
# helm indoors and doors both sides (8 tall ? the player is exactly 8
# cells; original-faithful exact fit); deck hatch dropping one storey
# into the machine hold (three 4x4 engines + two ballast blocks,
# protected inside) and again out the belly; pushers at stern AND bow;
# lift props hung beneath; turrets slung under the side pushers on
# struts (stern gun low, bow gun high).
#
# 'origin COL ROW' names which character is ship cell (0,0).

origin 48 32
